{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Data Analytics & Visualization\"\n",
        "subtitle: \"Data Analytics Foundations\"\n",
        "author: \"Victor Henriques, Ph.D.\"\n",
        "format:\n",
        "  revealjs:\n",
        "    theme: white\n",
        "    smaller: true\n",
        "    slide-number: c/t\n",
        "    transition: fade\n",
        "    center: false\n",
        "    width: 1600\n",
        "    height: 900\n",
        "    margin: 0.07\n",
        "    code-overflow: wrap\n",
        "    chalkboard: true\n",
        "    preview-links: auto\n",
        "    footer: \"Data Analytics & Visualization\"\n",
        "    logo: logo.svg\n",
        "execute:\n",
        "  echo: true\n",
        "  warning: false\n",
        "  error: false\n",
        "  cache: false\n",
        "jupyter: python3\n",
        "---"
      ],
      "id": "2da5b136"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| label: setup\n",
        "#| include: false\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import seaborn as sns\n",
        "\n",
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(42)\n",
        "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\", context=\"talk\")\n",
        "pd.set_option(\"display.max_columns\", 12)\n",
        "pd.set_option(\"display.width\", 120)"
      ],
      "id": "setup",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Data Analytics Foundations\n",
        "\n",
        "## The complete pandas workflow for Data Visualization\n",
        "\n",
        "- [Chapter 5: Getting Started with pandas](https://wesmckinney.com/book/pandas-basics)\n",
        "- [Chapter 7: Data Cleaning and Preparation](https://wesmckinney.com/book/data-cleaning)\n",
        "- [Chapter 8: Data Wrangling](https://wesmckinney.com/book/data-wrangling)\n",
        "- [Chapter 9: Plotting and Visualization](https://wesmckinney.com/book/plotting-and-visualization)\n",
        "- [Chapter 10: Data Aggregation and Group Operations](https://wesmckinney.com/book/data-aggregation)\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Apresente o módulo como um fluxo analítico completo. A ordem pedagógica difere da ordem numérica: primeiro compreender, preparar e estruturar; depois analisar e comunicar. Todos os dados são sintéticos. Tempo sugerido: 2 min.\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Chapter 5:** Understand\n",
        "2. **Chapter 7:** Prepare\n",
        "3. **Chapter 8:** Structure\n",
        "\n",
        "**Output:** validated, tidy, analysis-ready data.\n",
        "\n",
        "4. **Chapter 10:** Analyze\n",
        "5. **Chapter 9:** Communicate\n",
        "\n",
        "**Output:** validated summaries and defensible graphics.\n",
        "\n",
        "RAW DATA → INSPECT → CLEAN → COMBINE → RESHAPE → GROUP → SUMMARIZE → VISUALIZE → INTERPRET\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Learning objectives\n",
        "\n",
        "By the end of the module, students will be able to:\n",
        "\n",
        "- inspect and select labeled tabular data;\n",
        "- diagnose and document quality problems;\n",
        "- combine and reshape tables safely;\n",
        "- distinguish aggregation from transformation;\n",
        "- validate keys, denominators, and analytical outputs;\n",
        "- choose visual encodings based on a question;\n",
        "- create clear, accessible, and defensible visualizations.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Relacione cada objetivo a uma entrega observável. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Synthetic market data"
      ],
      "id": "3acc2bfd"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "raw = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"date\": [\"2026-01-02\", \"2026/01/02\", \"03-01-2026\", \"2026-01-03\",\n",
        "             \"2026-01-04\", \"2026-01-04\", \"2026-01-05\", \"bad-date\",\n",
        "             \"2026-01-06\", \"2026-01-07\", \"2026-01-07\", \"2026-01-08\"],\n",
        "    \"instrument\": [\" brent \", \"WTI\", \"ttf\", \"BRENT\", \"wti \", \"wti \",\n",
        "                   \"TTF\", \"TTF\", \"WTI\", \"UNKNOWN\", \"BRENT\", \"TTF\"],\n",
        "    \"market\": [\"Oil\", \"Oil\", \"gas\", \"OIL\", \"Oil\", \"Oil\",\n",
        "               \"Gas\", \"Gas\", \"Oil\", \"Other\", \"Oil\", \"Gas\"],\n",
        "    \"price\": [\"76.4\", \"72.1\", \"48.2\", \"77.0\", None, None,\n",
        "              \"-5\", \"49.1\", \"73.4\", \"80.0\", \"1,250.0\", \"50.2\"],\n",
        "    \"volume\": [120, 98, 84, 133, 105, 105, 90, 87, None, 40, 150, 91],\n",
        "    \"currency\": [\"USD\", \"USD\", \"EUR\", \"usd\", \"USD\", \"USD\",\n",
        "                 \"EUR\", \"EUR\", \"USD\", \"USD\", \"USD\", \"EUR\"]\n",
        "})\n",
        "metadata = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"instrument\": [\"BRENT\", \"WTI\", \"TTF\"],\n",
        "    \"region\": [\"Europe\", \"North America\", \"Europe\"],\n",
        "    \"category\": [\"Crude oil\", \"Crude oil\", \"Natural gas\"],\n",
        "    \"price_unit\": [\"USD/bbl\", \"USD/bbl\", \"EUR/MWh\"]\n",
        "})\n",
        "raw.head()"
      ],
      "id": "477f2b96",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Defina a unidade pretendida: um preço por instrumento e data. Peça aos alunos que identifiquem problemas sem ainda corrigi-los. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why the first chart is unreliable"
      ],
      "id": "5ec0987f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 10,
        "fig-height": 4.7
      },
      "source": [
        "#| fig-align: center\n",
        "raw_plot = raw.assign(\n",
        "    date_plot=pd.to_datetime(raw[\"date\"], errors=\"coerce\", format=\"mixed\", dayfirst=True),\n",
        "    price_plot=pd.to_numeric(raw[\"price\"], errors=\"coerce\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "for name, group in raw_plot.groupby(\"instrument\"):\n",
        "    ax.plot(group[\"date_plot\"], group[\"price_plot\"], marker=\"o\", label=repr(name))\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"Raw labels fragment the visual series\",\n",
        "       xlabel=\"Date\", ylabel=\"Reported price\")\n",
        "ax.legend(ncol=3, fontsize=9)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "e4199e64",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Destaque labels fragmentados, erros de parsing, duplicatas e unidades incompatíveis. O objetivo é criar necessidade para toda a sequência. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "# Getting started with Pandas\n",
        "\n",
        "## The observational unit comes first\n",
        "\n",
        "Before using pandas, answer:\n",
        "\n",
        "- What does one row represent?\n",
        "- What does each column represent?\n",
        "- Which columns identify a unique observation?\n",
        "- Which units are used?\n",
        "- Which labels carry analytical meaning?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "A unidade de observação orienta duplicatas, joins, agrupamentos e gráficos. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## `Series`: values plus labels"
      ],
      "id": "a133b666"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "latest = pd.Series(\n",
        "    [77.4, 73.5, 50.6],\n",
        "    index=[\"BRENT\", \"WTI\", \"TTF\"],\n",
        "    name=\"price\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "latest"
      ],
      "id": "504dc476",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "latest.loc[[\"BRENT\", \"TTF\"]]"
      ],
      "id": "bb1d35b7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "The string representation of a Series displayed interactively shows the index on the left and the values on the right. Since we did not specify an index for the data, a default one consisting of the integers 0 through N - 1 (where N is the length of the data) is created.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Label alignment protects meaning"
      ],
      "id": "18ee28ae"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "previous = pd.Series(\n",
        "    [49.8, 76.6, 72.7],\n",
        "    index=[\"TTF\", \"BRENT\", \"WTI\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "(latest - previous).round(2)"
      ],
      "id": "11cb3a93",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Order differs, but labels align correctly.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Often, you'll want to create a Series with an index identifying each data point with a label\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Missing labels create missing results"
      ],
      "id": "3d401989"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "partial = pd.Series({\"BRENT\": 76.6, \"WTI\": 72.7, \"HENRY\": 3.2})\n",
        "latest - partial"
      ],
      "id": "ccb5253f",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Alignment is safer than positional matching, but unmatched labels require investigation.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "A useful Series feature for many applications is that it automatically aligns by index label in arithmetic operations. If you have experience with databases, you can think about this as being similar to a join operation.\n",
        "\n",
        "Explique que NaN pode surgir do desalinhamento, não apenas de ausência original. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## `DataFrame`: labeled tabular structure"
      ],
      "id": "0302b817"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "snapshot = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"price\": latest,\n",
        "    \"volume\": pd.Series({\"BRENT\": 120, \"WTI\": 98, \"TTF\": 84})\n",
        "})\n",
        "snapshot"
      ],
      "id": "962c0fe6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "- rows have an index;\n",
        "- columns have names;\n",
        "- each column has a dtype;\n",
        "- columns may contain different data types.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "A DataFrame represents a rectangular table of data and contains an ordered, named collection of columns, each of which can be a different value type (numeric, string, Boolean, etc.). The DataFrame has both a row and column index; it can be thought of as a dictionary of Series all sharing the same index.\n",
        "\n",
        "There are many ways to construct a DataFrame, though one of the most common is from a dictionary of equal-length lists or NumPy arrays:\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Inspect before transforming\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.columns}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "ce3f368f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "raw.head(3)"
      ],
      "id": "fe517bf0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "raw.shape"
      ],
      "id": "9fe193e1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "raw.dtypes"
      ],
      "id": "603126f6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "11cb683d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "raw.tail(3)"
      ],
      "id": "2e1fe6b7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "raw.info()"
      ],
      "id": "b895ff08",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Explique por que head não basta. Sample pode revelar erros que aparecem no meio da tabela. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Select by label and position\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "48db624b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "raw.loc[0:2, [\"instrument\", \"price\"]]"
      ],
      "id": "63bd68cc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "`loc` uses labels and includes the endpoint.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "07c87fa1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "raw.iloc[0:3, [1, 3]]"
      ],
      "id": "fb6581f7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "`iloc` uses positions and excludes the stop.\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Os resultados coincidem aqui, mas as regras são distintas. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Boolean filtering and explicit copies"
      ],
      "id": "95cb0936"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "oil = raw.loc[\n",
        "    raw[\"market\"].str.strip().str.casefold().eq(\"oil\"),\n",
        "    [\"date\", \"instrument\", \"price\", \"volume\"]\n",
        "].copy()\n",
        "oil.head()"
      ],
      "id": "cc414dfa",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Use `.copy()` when the subset will later be modified.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Explique máscara, seleção nos dois eixos e intenção de cópia. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ## Checkpoint 1 -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Predict the result: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ```python -->\n",
        "<!-- quiz = pd.DataFrame( -->\n",
        "<!--     {\"price\": [10, 20, 30], \"volume\": [2, 4, 6]}, -->\n",
        "<!--     index=[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"] -->\n",
        "<!-- ) -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- quiz.loc[\"A\":\"B\", [\"price\"]] -->\n",
        "<!-- quiz.iloc[0:2, 0:1] -->\n",
        "<!-- ``` -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- What is equal, and what rule differs? -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ::: {.notes} -->\n",
        "<!-- Dê um minuto em duplas. Ambos retornam DataFrame 2 por 1, mas loc inclui o label final e iloc exclui a posição stop. Tempo: 3 min. -->\n",
        "<!-- ::: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ## Checkpoint 1 -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Predict the result: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ```{python} -->\n",
        "<!-- quiz = pd.DataFrame( -->\n",
        "<!--     {\"price\": [10, 20, 30], \"volume\": [2, 4, 6]}, -->\n",
        "<!--     index=[\"A\", \"B\", \"C\"] -->\n",
        "<!-- ) -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- quiz.loc[\"A\":\"B\", [\"price\"]] -->\n",
        "<!-- quiz.iloc[0:2, 0:1] -->\n",
        "<!-- ``` -->\n",
        "\n",
        "## Constructing Series and DataFrames\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "4831cdb3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "series_from_dict = pd.Series({\n",
        "    \"BRENT\": 77.4, \"WTI\": 73.5, \"TTF\": 50.6\n",
        "}, name=\"price\")\n",
        "series_from_dict"
      ],
      "id": "c3ae38f6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "787cff3b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "frame_from_records = pd.DataFrame([\n",
        "    {\"instrument\": \"BRENT\", \"price\": 77.4},\n",
        "    {\"instrument\": \"WTI\", \"price\": 73.5}\n",
        "])\n",
        "frame_from_records"
      ],
      "id": "119e29ca",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "Choose a constructor that preserves the meaning of records, variables, and labels.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Compare dicionário como mapping index-value com lista de registros. Pergunte qual estrutura representa observações nas linhas. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Index objects are structural metadata"
      ],
      "id": "1a6a785c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "idx = pd.Index([\"BRENT\", \"WTI\", \"TTF\"], name=\"instrument\")\n",
        "print(\"unique:\", idx.is_unique)\n",
        "print(\"membership:\", idx.isin([\"BRENT\", \"TTF\"]))\n",
        "print(\"union:\", idx.union(pd.Index([\"HENRY\"])).tolist())"
      ],
      "id": "3c52cf30",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "- indexes are immutable;\n",
        "- indexes support set operations;\n",
        "- uniqueness affects selection, joins, and reshaping;\n",
        "- index names document analytical meaning.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Apresente Index como parte da estrutura, não como mero número de linha. Unicidade será reutilizada em joins e pivots. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Reindexing is alignment to a target structure"
      ],
      "id": "991bc2b5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "target = [\"TTF\", \"BRENT\", \"WTI\", \"HENRY\"]\n",
        "latest.reindex(target)"
      ],
      "id": "2945c53c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "latest.reindex(target, fill_value=0)"
      ],
      "id": "bdefe1d8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.callout-warning}\n",
        "A fill value changes the data-generating assumption. Zero is not a neutral replacement for a missing market price.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "An important method on pandas objects is reindex, which means to create a new object with the values rearranged to align with the new index. Calling reindex on this Series rearranges the data according to the new index, introducing missing values if any index values were not already present\n",
        "\n",
        "For ordered data like time series, you may want to do some interpolation or filling of values when reindexing. The method option allows us to do this, using a method such as ffill, which forward-fills the values:\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Dropping labels does not validate them"
      ],
      "id": "784012d2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "snapshot.drop(index=\"TTF\")"
      ],
      "id": "1a1aec3d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "snapshot.drop(columns=\"volume\")"
      ],
      "id": "dcc45e00",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "`drop` returns a new object by default. Removing a row or column is a structural action, not evidence that exclusion is analytically justified.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Conecte drop à governança: remover é fácil, justificar é a parte analítica. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Selection syntax and output dimensionality\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "f9b64a26"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "snapshot[\"price\"]"
      ],
      "id": "6532749d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "A `Series`: one-dimensional.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "3aa100a0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "snapshot[[\"price\"]]"
      ],
      "id": "666863c7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "A `DataFrame`: two-dimensional.\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "The brackets determine output dimensionality, which affects downstream methods and plotting APIs.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Este detalhe é essencial para iniciantes. Mostre shape e tipo dos dois resultados. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Integer labels are not positions"
      ],
      "id": "d37a6ab8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "integer_indexed = pd.Series([76.4, 72.1, 48.2], index=[10, 20, 30])\n",
        "print(\"label 10:\", integer_indexed.loc[10])\n",
        "print(\"position 0:\", integer_indexed.iloc[0])"
      ],
      "id": "fe76e4e0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Use `loc` and `iloc` explicitly to avoid ambiguity.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Explique por que s[0] não é uma forma robusta de comunicar intenção quando o índice é inteiro. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Arithmetic aligns both axes"
      ],
      "id": "de67d535"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "left = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "    {\"BRENT\": [76.0, 77.0], \"WTI\": [72.0, 73.0]},\n",
        "    index=[\"day_1\", \"day_2\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "right = pd.DataFrame(\n",
        "    {\"WTI\": [71.5, 72.5], \"TTF\": [49.0, 50.0]},\n",
        "    index=[\"day_2\", \"day_3\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "left - right"
      ],
      "id": "0a418009",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Rows and columns both align; only common labels have computable differences.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "The internal data alignment introduces missing values in the label locations that don’t overlap. Missing values will then propagate in further arithmetic computations.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Arithmetic with fill values"
      ],
      "id": "336b36a0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "left.add(right, fill_value=0)"
      ],
      "id": "d7813125",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "`fill_value` is applied during alignment, but does not make zero substantively correct.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "In arithmetic operations between differently indexed objects, you might want to fill with a special value, like 0, when an axis label is found in one object but not the other. \n",
        "\n",
        "Using the add method on left, I pass right and an argument to fill_value, which substitutes the passed value for any missing values in the operation.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Function application and elementwise mapping"
      ],
      "id": "bc0345f2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "numeric_frame = snapshot.loc[:, [\"price\", \"volume\"]]\n",
        "range_by_column = numeric_frame.apply(lambda s: s.max() - s.min())\n",
        "range_by_column"
      ],
      "id": "3e1c4665",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "numeric_frame.map(lambda x: f\"{x:.1f}\")"
      ],
      "id": "72cbc85a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "- `apply`: operate along an axis;\n",
        "- `map`: operate element by element;\n",
        "- prefer vectorized methods when available.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Another frequent operation is applying a function on one-dimensional arrays to each column or row. DataFrame’s apply method.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Sorting data versus ranking values"
      ],
      "id": "e4d57bfd"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print(latest.sort_values(ascending=False))\n",
        "print(latest.rank(ascending=False, method=\"dense\"))"
      ],
      "id": "b8627213",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Sorting rearranges observations; ranking assigns an order statistic.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Sorting a dataset by some criterion is another important built-in operation. To sort lexicographically by row or column label, use the sort_index method, which returns a new, sorted object.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Duplicate labels change selection behavior"
      ],
      "id": "0e628251"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "duplicate_index = pd.Series(\n",
        "    [76.4, 76.7, 72.1], index=[\"BRENT\", \"BRENT\", \"WTI\"]\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(\"is unique:\", duplicate_index.index.is_unique)\n",
        "duplicate_index.loc[\"BRENT\"]"
      ],
      "id": "763af9b0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "A label may return one scalar or multiple values depending on index uniqueness.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Este comportamento torna pipelines frágeis. Verifique is_unique quando a chave deveria ser exclusiva. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Reductions and missing-data defaults"
      ],
      "id": "e29cc6ac"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "summary_demo = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"price\": [76.4, np.nan, 72.1],\n",
        "    \"volume\": [120, 98, np.nan]\n",
        "})\n",
        "print(summary_demo.sum())\n",
        "print(summary_demo.mean())\n",
        "print(summary_demo.sum(skipna=False))"
      ],
      "id": "2154527c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Many pandas reductions skip missing values by default. The denominator still needs interpretation.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Mostre que um número pode ser produzido apesar de cobertura incompleta. Conecte ao capítulo 10. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Unique values, frequencies, and membership"
      ],
      "id": "2fd4a085"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "labels_demo = pd.Series([\"Oil\", \"Gas\", \"Oil\", None, \"oil\"])\n",
        "print(labels_demo.unique())\n",
        "print(labels_demo.value_counts(dropna=False))\n",
        "print(labels_demo.isin([\"Oil\", \"Gas\"]))"
      ],
      "id": "cdf48eed",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "These operations are essential for auditing categories before legends, colors, and facets are created.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Mostre que Oil e oil viram categorias visuais distintas. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "# Data Cleaning and Preparation\n",
        "\n",
        "## Quality problems are not synonyms\n",
        "\n",
        "| Problem | Meaning | First response |\n",
        "|---|---|---|\n",
        "| Missing | value not observed | inspect pattern |\n",
        "| Invalid | violates a domain rule | verify or quarantine |\n",
        "| Duplicate | repeated analytical unit | define the key |\n",
        "| Inconsistent | same concept, different encoding | standardize |\n",
        "| Outlier | unusual but possibly valid | investigate |\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Outlier não é automaticamente erro. Limpeza começa por diagnóstico. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Diagnose quality"
      ],
      "id": "ffd8f48d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "quality = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"dtype\": raw.dtypes.astype(str),\n",
        "    \"missing\": raw.isna().sum(),\n",
        "    \"unique\": raw.nunique(dropna=True)\n",
        "})\n",
        "quality"
      ],
      "id": "8e017a98",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "print(\"exact duplicates:\", raw.duplicated().sum())\n",
        "print(raw[\"instrument\"].unique().tolist())"
      ],
      "id": "b0b7a3ee",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Mostre como object pode esconder datas e números. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Missingness is data"
      ],
      "id": "bf63370d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "missing = raw.isna()\n",
        "missing.sum().sort_values(ascending=False)"
      ],
      "id": "f9ecb7be",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 9,
        "fig-height": 4.5
      },
      "source": [
        "#| fig-align: center\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.heatmap(missing.T, cbar=False,\n",
        "            cmap=[\"#F2F2F2\", \"#D55E00\"], ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"Missingness in the raw table\", xlabel=\"Row\", ylabel=\"Variable\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "5c9ed655",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "A ausência pode revelar falha de coleta. Valores que falham no parsing também criam ausências novas. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Drop, fill, or retain?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "ff82a33e"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "raw.dropna(subset=[\"price\"]).shape"
      ],
      "id": "12a378f1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Removal discards other observed information.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "f16d2fd3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "raw.assign(\n",
        "    volume=raw[\"volume\"].fillna(raw[\"volume\"].median())\n",
        ").loc[raw[\"volume\"].isna()]"
      ],
      "id": "99a99e40",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Filling introduces an assumption.\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Peça mecanismo, objetivo analítico e consequência antes de decidir. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Parse types and expose failures"
      ],
      "id": "b1ea555f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "parsed = raw.assign(\n",
        "    date_parsed=pd.to_datetime(\n",
        "        raw[\"date\"], errors=\"coerce\", format=\"mixed\", dayfirst=True\n",
        "    ),\n",
        "    price_parsed=pd.to_numeric(\n",
        "        raw[\"price\"].astype(\"string\").str.replace(\",\", \"\", regex=False),\n",
        "        errors=\"coerce\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "parsed.loc[:, [\"date\", \"date_parsed\", \"price\", \"price_parsed\"]].head(6)"
      ],
      "id": "3d9218a2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Coerce torna a falha explícita, mas não a explica. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Standardize strings and categories"
      ],
      "id": "1b620711"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "clean = (\n",
        "    parsed.assign(\n",
        "        instrument=parsed[\"instrument\"].str.strip().str.upper(),\n",
        "        market=parsed[\"market\"].str.strip().str.title(),\n",
        "        currency=parsed[\"currency\"].str.strip().str.upper()\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .drop(columns=[\"date\", \"price\"])\n",
        "    .rename(columns={\"date_parsed\": \"date\", \"price_parsed\": \"price\"})\n",
        ")\n",
        "clean.loc[:, [\"instrument\", \"market\", \"currency\"]].drop_duplicates()"
      ],
      "id": "fffe86cf",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Mostre strip, upper, title, drop e rename. Inspecione valores únicos após padronizar. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Replace, map, and categorize"
      ],
      "id": "21286b9b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "clean = clean.assign(\n",
        "    currency=clean[\"currency\"].replace({\"US$\": \"USD\"}),\n",
        "    market_group=clean[\"market\"].map({\n",
        "        \"Oil\": \"Liquid energy\", \"Gas\": \"Gaseous energy\", \"Other\": \"Other\"\n",
        "    }),\n",
        "    volume_band=pd.cut(\n",
        "        clean[\"volume\"], bins=[0, 90, 120, np.inf],\n",
        "        labels=[\"low\", \"medium\", \"high\"]\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "clean.loc[:, [\"market\", \"market_group\", \"volume\", \"volume_band\"]].head()"
      ],
      "id": "7f94a122",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Map pode criar ausência para chaves não previstas. Cut reduz informação e exige justificativa. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Duplicates require an analytical key"
      ],
      "id": "bf0914a8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "exact_dup = clean.duplicated()\n",
        "key_dup = clean.duplicated(subset=[\"date\", \"instrument\"], keep=False)\n",
        "clean.loc[exact_dup | key_dup,\n",
        "          [\"date\", \"instrument\", \"price\", \"volume\"]]"
      ],
      "id": "03630d96",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "dedup = clean.drop_duplicates(\n",
        "    subset=[\"date\", \"instrument\", \"price\", \"volume\"], keep=\"first\"\n",
        ").copy()"
      ],
      "id": "a934ada2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Pergunte se uma linha é preço diário, cotação ou evento de publicação. A chave depende da resposta. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Invalid versus unusual"
      ],
      "id": "c4a208f7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "invalid = dedup[\"price\"].le(0)\n",
        "unusual = dedup[\"price\"].gt(500)\n",
        "dedup.loc[invalid | unusual,\n",
        "          [\"date\", \"instrument\", \"price\", \"currency\"]]"
      ],
      "id": "ebe48a8b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "- non-positive is invalid under this teaching rule;\n",
        "- above 500 is unusual and requires investigation;\n",
        "- negative prices may be valid in some real markets.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Explicite que a regra é contextual e didática. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ## Checkpoint 2 -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- For each case, choose **retain, flag, correct, fill, or remove**: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- 1. no trade occurred; -->\n",
        "<!-- 2. instrument has trailing spaces; -->\n",
        "<!-- 3. duplicated ingestion event; -->\n",
        "<!-- 4. extreme but verified market movement; -->\n",
        "<!-- 5. date cannot be parsed. -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- State what must be recorded. -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ::: {.notes} -->\n",
        "<!-- Avalie justificativa e rastreabilidade, não apenas a resposta. Tempo: 4 min. -->\n",
        "<!-- ::: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Missing values must be interpreted by dtype"
      ],
      "id": "6dcdd7ba"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "nullable = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"trades\": pd.Series([10, None, 12], dtype=\"Int64\"),\n",
        "    \"active\": pd.Series([True, None, False], dtype=\"boolean\"),\n",
        "    \"instrument\": pd.Series([\"BRENT\", None, \"WTI\"], dtype=\"string\")\n",
        "})\n",
        "nullable.dtypes"
      ],
      "id": "4abd485a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Pandas extension dtypes preserve missing integers, Booleans, and strings without coercing everything to generic objects.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Apresente pd.NA e tipos anuláveis. Explique que dtype influencia operações, memória e visualização. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## `dropna` has several decision thresholds"
      ],
      "id": "c93d80a6"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "missing_demo = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"price\": [76.4, np.nan, np.nan],\n",
        "    \"volume\": [120, 98, np.nan],\n",
        "    \"currency\": [\"USD\", \"USD\", None]\n",
        "})\n",
        "print(missing_demo.dropna())\n",
        "print(missing_demo.dropna(how=\"all\"))\n",
        "print(missing_demo.dropna(thresh=2))"
      ],
      "id": "23d24e53",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The threshold encodes how much observed information is required to retain a row.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Diferencie any, all e thresh. A decisão depende das colunas essenciais. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Forward fill and backward fill encode ordering assumptions"
      ],
      "id": "211f1518"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "time_demo = pd.Series(\n",
        "    [76.4, np.nan, np.nan, 77.1],\n",
        "    index=pd.date_range(\"2026-01-01\", periods=4)\n",
        ")\n",
        "print(time_demo.ffill(limit=1))\n",
        "print(time_demo.bfill(limit=1))"
      ],
      "id": "7b16f47a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Carry-forward methods require a meaningful order and should use limits when long gaps are not defensible.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Evite recomendar ffill automaticamente para preços. Discuta hipótese de persistência e limite. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Replacing values and renaming axes"
      ],
      "id": "e390c55d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "code_demo = pd.DataFrame({\"mkt\": [\"OIL\", \"NG\", \"N/A\"]})\n",
        "code_demo = (\n",
        "    code_demo.replace({\"N/A\": pd.NA, \"NG\": \"GAS\"})\n",
        "    .rename(columns={\"mkt\": \"market\"})\n",
        ")\n",
        "code_demo"
      ],
      "id": "cfd9d34b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Renaming improves semantics; replacing changes values. Keep those operations conceptually separate.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Diferencie mudar o nome da variável de recodificar observações. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Detecting and filtering unusual values"
      ],
      "id": "9cd8d44a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "values = pd.Series([72, 73, 74, 1200, 75], name=\"price\")\n",
        "center = values.median()\n",
        "mad = (values - center).abs().median()\n",
        "robust_score = 0.6745 * (values - center) / mad\n",
        "pd.DataFrame({\"price\": values, \"robust_score\": robust_score.round(2)})"
      ],
      "id": "3a6535f7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "A statistical flag is a prompt for investigation, not proof of error.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Introduza robust z-score apenas como diagnóstico. Dados de mercado podem ter regimes e caudas pesadas. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Permutation and sampling"
      ],
      "id": "340f1e6b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "sample_demo = clean.sample(n=4, random_state=42)\n",
        "permuted_demo = clean.iloc[rng.permutation(len(clean))[:4]]\n",
        "print(sample_demo.index.tolist())\n",
        "print(permuted_demo.index.tolist())"
      ],
      "id": "d6a3251c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Sampling supports inspection and validation; reproducibility requires a fixed random state or generator.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Conecte sample à inspeção além de head. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Dummy variables for categorical encodings"
      ],
      "id": "38e83b1d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pd.get_dummies(\n",
        "    clean[\"market\"], prefix=\"market\", dtype=\"int8\"\n",
        ").head()"
      ],
      "id": "ecd022d7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Dummy variables are useful for modeling, but visualization libraries often work directly with categorical columns.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Diferencie necessidade de modeling de necessidade de plotting. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Vectorized string methods and regular expressions"
      ],
      "id": "b1423b2a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "contracts = pd.Series(\n",
        "    [\"BRENT_M1\", \"WTI-M2\", \"TTF_Q1\", None], dtype=\"string\"\n",
        ")\n",
        "contracts.str.extract(\n",
        "    r\"(?P<instrument>[A-Z]+)[_-](?P<tenor>[A-Z]\\d)\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "a833a426",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "contracts.str.contains(r\"M\\d\", na=False)"
      ],
      "id": "d5b3cb99",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Pandas string methods apply text operations across arrays while handling missing values.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Explique grupos nomeados e na=False. Regex deve ser testada com casos válidos e inválidos. Tempo: 4 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "# Data Wrangling: Join, Combine, and Reshape\n",
        "\n",
        "## `concat` is not a relational join"
      ],
      "id": "35abd50b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "part_a = dedup.iloc[:4].copy()\n",
        "part_b = dedup.iloc[4:8].copy()\n",
        "combined = pd.concat([part_a, part_b], ignore_index=True)\n",
        "combined.shape"
      ],
      "id": "cf7f607d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "`concat` appends or aligns objects along an axis.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Diferencie empilhamento de associação por chave. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Keys and cardinality\n",
        "\n",
        "| Relationship | Meaning |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| one-to-one | each key occurs once on both sides |\n",
        "| many-to-one | many observations reference one metadata row |\n",
        "| one-to-many | one left key matches several right rows |\n",
        "| many-to-many | duplicated keys may multiply rows |\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Use observações diárias e metadata como exemplo de muitos-para-um. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Anatomy of a validated merge"
      ],
      "id": "4c58ab9f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "merged = dedup.merge(\n",
        "    metadata,\n",
        "    on=\"instrument\",\n",
        "    how=\"left\",\n",
        "    validate=\"many_to_one\",\n",
        "    indicator=True\n",
        ")\n",
        "assert len(merged) == len(dedup)\n",
        "merged.loc[:, [\"instrument\", \"region\", \"price_unit\", \"_merge\"]].head(8)"
      ],
      "id": "44868aca",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Explique chave, tipo de join, contrato de cardinalidade e coluna de auditoria. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Join types as set logic\n",
        "\n",
        "```text\n",
        "LEFT:  A B C        RIGHT:  B C D\n",
        "inner → B C         left  → A B C\n",
        "right → B C D       outer → A B C D\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "| Join | Analytical question |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| inner | What overlaps? |\n",
        "| left | What happened to every observation? |\n",
        "| right | Which reference keys lack observations? |\n",
        "| outer | Where are all mismatches? |\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Lembre que o diagrama mostra chaves únicas, não o número final de linhas com duplicatas. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Many-to-many risk"
      ],
      "id": "fa372e1c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "bad_metadata = pd.concat([\n",
        "    metadata,\n",
        "    metadata.loc[metadata[\"instrument\"].eq(\"BRENT\")]\n",
        "], ignore_index=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    dedup.merge(bad_metadata, on=\"instrument\", how=\"left\",\n",
        "                validate=\"many_to_one\")\n",
        "except pd.errors.MergeError as err:\n",
        "    print(type(err).__name__, \"-\", str(err).split(\";\")[0])"
      ],
      "id": "5c97fb1e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Validate transforma uma suposição em contrato executável. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Audit unmatched records"
      ],
      "id": "897b2ec3"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "merged[\"_merge\"].value_counts()"
      ],
      "id": "ed038d46",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "unmatched = merged.loc[merged[\"_merge\"].ne(\"both\"), \"instrument\"].unique()\n",
        "unmatched"
      ],
      "id": "d842b84b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Never remove unmatched records before making them visible.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "UNKNOWN deve ser auditado antes de ser excluído da tabela analítica. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Wide versus long\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "**Wide**\n",
        "\n",
        "| date | BRENT | WTI | TTF |\n",
        "|---|---:|---:|---:|\n",
        "| Jan 2 | 76.4 | 72.1 | 48.2 |\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "**Long**\n",
        "\n",
        "| date | instrument | price |\n",
        "|---|---|---:|\n",
        "| Jan 2 | BRENT | 76.4 |\n",
        "| Jan 2 | WTI | 72.1 |\n",
        "| Jan 2 | TTF | 48.2 |\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Formato é estrutura: long facilita mapeamentos visuais e agrupamentos. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## `melt`, `pivot`, and `pivot_table`"
      ],
      "id": "a6a7e13f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "wide = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"date\": [\"2026-01-02\", \"2026-01-03\"],\n",
        "    \"BRENT\": [76.4, 77.0], \"WTI\": [72.1, 72.8], \"TTF\": [48.2, 48.7]\n",
        "})\n",
        "long = wide.melt(id_vars=\"date\", var_name=\"instrument\", value_name=\"price\")\n",
        "long.head(3)"
      ],
      "id": "57a830ef",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "long.pivot(index=\"date\", columns=\"instrument\", values=\"price\").head(3)"
      ],
      "id": "100a4c9d",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Melt reorganiza sem agregar. Pivot exige pares exclusivos. Pivot_table agregaria colisões. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## MultiIndex, `stack`, and `unstack`"
      ],
      "id": "12d170c7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "small = merged.dropna(subset=[\"date\", \"price\"]).set_index(\n",
        "    [\"instrument\", \"date\"]\n",
        ")[\"price\"].head(6)\n",
        "wide_indexed = small.unstack(\"instrument\")\n",
        "wide_indexed.head(3)"
      ],
      "id": "b8706c03",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "wide_indexed.stack(future_stack=True).head(3)"
      ],
      "id": "7a2b7b41",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Conteúdo útil, não central. Unstack move nível do índice para colunas; stack faz o inverso. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Reordering and sorting index levels"
      ],
      "id": "d03841ea"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "hier = merged.dropna(subset=[\"date\"]).set_index(\n",
        "    [\"instrument\", \"date\"]\n",
        ").sort_index()\n",
        "print(hier.index.names)\n",
        "hier.swaplevel(\"instrument\", \"date\").sort_index().head(3)"
      ],
      "id": "74db963c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Index-level order changes which partial selections and grouped operations are natural.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Conecte ordem do MultiIndex à forma de consulta. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Merge on differently named keys"
      ],
      "id": "205603b5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "left_keys = pd.DataFrame({\"ticker\": [\"BRENT\", \"WTI\", \"TTF\"]})\n",
        "right_keys = pd.DataFrame({\"instrument\": [\"BRENT\", \"WTI\", \"TTF\"],\n",
        "                           \"category\": [\"Oil\", \"Oil\", \"Gas\"]})\n",
        "left_keys.merge(\n",
        "    right_keys, left_on=\"ticker\", right_on=\"instrument\",\n",
        "    validate=\"one_to_one\"\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "d1e1b47b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Mostre left_on e right_on. Preserve ambas as colunas até confirmar equivalência semântica. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Merge using indexes"
      ],
      "id": "4ee91d58"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "left_indexed = left_keys.set_index(\"ticker\")\n",
        "right_indexed = right_keys.set_index(\"instrument\")\n",
        "left_indexed.join(right_indexed, how=\"left\", validate=\"one_to_one\")"
      ],
      "id": "f7d245f7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Index-based joins are concise, but column-based merge often exposes key semantics more clearly.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Discuta legibilidade e não apenas concisão. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Concatenation keys preserve provenance"
      ],
      "id": "32083306"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "jan = pd.DataFrame({\"price\": [76.4, 72.1]}, index=[\"BRENT\", \"WTI\"])\n",
        "feb = pd.DataFrame({\"price\": [77.2, 73.0]}, index=[\"BRENT\", \"WTI\"])\n",
        "pd.concat({\"January\": jan, \"February\": feb}, names=[\"month\", \"instrument\"])"
      ],
      "id": "1ee8a8e7",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Keys create a hierarchical index that records the source of each block.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Mostre como concat pode preservar proveniência. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Overlapping columns and suffixes"
      ],
      "id": "8c4ee988"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "quotes_a = pd.DataFrame({\"instrument\": [\"BRENT\"], \"price\": [76.4]})\n",
        "quotes_b = pd.DataFrame({\"instrument\": [\"BRENT\"], \"price\": [76.6]})\n",
        "quotes_a.merge(quotes_b, on=\"instrument\", suffixes=(\"_source_a\", \"_source_b\"))"
      ],
      "id": "54abd217",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Suffixes avoid ambiguous names but do not resolve conflicting definitions.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Duas colunas chamadas price podem ter timestamp, fonte ou metodologia diferentes. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## `combine_first` patches aligned missing values"
      ],
      "id": "f6be50a1"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "primary = pd.Series([76.4, np.nan, 78.0], index=[\"d1\", \"d2\", \"d3\"])\n",
        "backup = pd.Series([76.3, 77.1, 77.9], index=[\"d1\", \"d2\", \"d3\"])\n",
        "primary.combine_first(backup)"
      ],
      "id": "2bba2c15",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The operation preserves primary values and uses backup values only where the primary is missing.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Exija uma política de fonte e uma flag de proveniência em aplicações reais. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Class 1 integrated pipeline"
      ],
      "id": "be46c932"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "working = raw.assign(\n",
        "    date=lambda d: pd.to_datetime(d[\"date\"], errors=\"coerce\", format=\"mixed\", dayfirst=True),\n",
        "    instrument=lambda d: d[\"instrument\"].str.strip().str.upper(),\n",
        "    market=lambda d: d[\"market\"].str.strip().str.title(),\n",
        "    currency=lambda d: d[\"currency\"].str.strip().str.upper(),\n",
        "    price=lambda d: pd.to_numeric(\n",
        "        d[\"price\"].astype(\"string\").str.replace(\",\", \"\", regex=False),\n",
        "        errors=\"coerce\"\n",
        "    )\n",
        ").drop_duplicates()"
      ],
      "id": "17e6ec4e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "A primeira parte corrige estrutura e tipos, sem ainda remover falhas. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Preserve an audit trail"
      ],
      "id": "024834e2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "working = working.assign(\n",
        "    invalid_date=working[\"date\"].isna(),\n",
        "    missing_price=working[\"price\"].isna(),\n",
        "    nonpositive_price=working[\"price\"].le(0).fillna(False)\n",
        ")\n",
        "rejected = working.loc[\n",
        "    working[[\"invalid_date\", \"nonpositive_price\"]].any(axis=1)\n",
        "].copy()\n",
        "valid = working.loc[\n",
        "    ~working[[\"invalid_date\", \"nonpositive_price\"]].any(axis=1)\n",
        "].copy()"
      ],
      "id": "a1edb230",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Separar rejeitados mantém rastreabilidade. Preço ausente não é rejeitado automaticamente. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Complete and validate Class 1 output"
      ],
      "id": "c85e85e4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "valid[\"price_imputed\"] = valid[\"price\"].isna()\n",
        "valid[\"price\"] = valid.groupby(\"instrument\")[\"price\"].transform(\n",
        "    lambda s: s.fillna(s.median())\n",
        ")\n",
        "analysis_data = valid.merge(\n",
        "    metadata, on=\"instrument\", how=\"left\",\n",
        "    validate=\"many_to_one\", indicator=True\n",
        ")\n",
        "chart_ready = analysis_data.loc[analysis_data[\"_merge\"].eq(\"both\")].drop(columns=\"_merge\")\n",
        "assert chart_ready[[\"date\", \"instrument\", \"price\", \"price_unit\"]].notna().all().all()\n",
        "assert metadata[\"instrument\"].is_unique\n",
        "chart_ready.head(2)"
      ],
      "id": "daf5aafc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "A mediana por instrumento é uma hipótese didática. A saída é validada, tidy e pronta para análise. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ## End of Class 1 -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ### Deliverable -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- > A validated, tidy, analysis-ready dataset with explicit units, keys, and quality flags. -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ### Exit ticket -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- - What is one assumption in the pipeline? -->\n",
        "<!-- - Which assertion protects a key relationship? -->\n",
        "<!-- - Which records are absent from `chart_ready`, and why? -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ::: {.notes} -->\n",
        "<!-- Use como fechamento da primeira aula e ponte para a segunda. Tempo: 4 min. -->\n",
        "<!-- ::: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- # Class 2 -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ## From analysis-ready data to visual evidence -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- **Chapter 10 → Chapter 9** -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ::: {.notes} -->\n",
        "<!-- Relembre a tabela chart_ready e a unidade de observação. Tempo: 1 min. -->\n",
        "<!-- ::: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "# Data Aggregation and Group Operations\n",
        "\n",
        "## Split–apply–combine\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Split** rows using one or more keys.\n",
        "2. **Apply** an aggregation, transformation, filter, or custom operation.\n",
        "3. **Combine** the results into a pandas object."
      ],
      "id": "e95f2612"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "grouped = chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\")\n",
        "type(grouped).__name__"
      ],
      "id": "278b2461",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "O GroupBy representa um plano até receber uma operação. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Define the grouping question\n",
        "\n",
        "Before calling `groupby`, specify:\n",
        "\n",
        "- observational unit;\n",
        "- grouping key;\n",
        "- outcome variable;\n",
        "- desired statistic;\n",
        "- denominator;\n",
        "- expected result shape.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Evite ensinar groupby como chamada mecânica. Pergunta e denominador vêm antes. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## First summaries and named aggregation"
      ],
      "id": "faf5e956"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "summary = (\n",
        "    chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\", as_index=False)\n",
        "    .agg(\n",
        "        rows=(\"price\", \"size\"),\n",
        "        observed_prices=(\"price\", \"count\"),\n",
        "        mean_price=(\"price\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "        median_price=(\"price\", \"median\"),\n",
        "        price_sd=(\"price\", \"std\"),\n",
        "        total_volume=(\"volume\", \"sum\")\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "summary.round(2)"
      ],
      "id": "5c51094a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Count exclui ausência; size conta linhas. Named aggregation produz nomes claros. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Aggregation reduces; transformation preserves\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.columns}\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "d6df7385"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\")[\"price\"].mean()"
      ],
      "id": "22120a64",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "One result per group.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}"
      ],
      "id": "46b50f19"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\")[\"price\"].transform(\"mean\").head()"
      ],
      "id": "cc95e551",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "One aligned result per row.\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Use o shape como critério principal. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Within-group transformation"
      ],
      "id": "85737353"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "chart_ready = chart_ready.sort_values([\"instrument\", \"date\"]).copy()\n",
        "chart_ready[\"return_pct\"] = chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\")[\"price\"].pct_change(\n",
        "    fill_method=None\n",
        ").mul(100)\n",
        "chart_ready[\"price_z\"] = chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\")[\"price\"].transform(\n",
        "    lambda s: (s - s.mean()) / s.std()\n",
        ")\n",
        "chart_ready.loc[:, [\"date\", \"instrument\", \"price\", \"return_pct\", \"price_z\"]].head(7)"
      ],
      "id": "d92aebe0",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Ordenação é parte da validade. Z-score compara posição relativa; retorno compara mudança percentual. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Filter groups and use `apply` selectively"
      ],
      "id": "8eaaa318"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "covered = chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\").filter(\n",
        "    lambda g: g[\"price\"].notna().mean() >= 0.95\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "def top_volume_rows(group, n=2):\n",
        "    return group.nlargest(n, \"volume\")\n",
        "\n",
        "top_volume = chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\", group_keys=False).apply(\n",
        "    top_volume_rows, include_groups=False\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "faaa0dd1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Use specialized operations before `apply`.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Filter decide sobre grupos inteiros. Apply é flexível, mas menos previsível. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Pivot tables and crosstabs"
      ],
      "id": "c3d886d0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "chart_ready[\"week\"] = ((chart_ready[\"date\"].dt.day - 1) // 7 + 1).astype(int)\n",
        "weekly_price = chart_ready.pivot_table(\n",
        "    index=\"instrument\", columns=\"week\", values=\"price_z\",\n",
        "    aggfunc=\"mean\", observed=True\n",
        ").astype(float)\n",
        "weekly_price.round(2)"
      ],
      "id": "888db715",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Pivot table agrega e reorganiza. Crosstab mostra proporções dentro de cada instrumento; explicite o denominador. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Pivot tables and crosstabs"
      ],
      "id": "976414b7"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "pd.crosstab(\n",
        "    chart_ready[\"instrument\"], chart_ready[\"price_imputed\"], normalize=\"index\"\n",
        ").round(2)"
      ],
      "id": "9461ebf2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Pivot table agrega e reorganiza. Crosstab mostra proporções dentro de cada instrumento; explicite o denominador. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Validate grouped results"
      ],
      "id": "0d24ecab"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "check = chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\").agg(\n",
        "    rows=(\"price\", \"size\"),\n",
        "    observed=(\"price\", \"count\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "assert check[\"rows\"].sum() == len(chart_ready)\n",
        "assert check[\"observed\"].sum() == chart_ready[\"price\"].notna().sum()\n",
        "assert check[\"observed\"].le(check[\"rows\"]).all()\n",
        "check"
      ],
      "id": "75aa4a47",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Valide denominadores, cobertura e forma do resultado. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ## Checkpoint 3 -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Choose the most specific operation: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- 1. one mean per instrument; -->\n",
        "<!-- 2. subtract each instrument's own mean from every row; -->\n",
        "<!-- 3. retain instruments with sufficient coverage; -->\n",
        "<!-- 4. obtain two rows with highest volume per group; -->\n",
        "<!-- 5. create several named summaries. -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ::: {.notes} -->\n",
        "<!-- Respostas: agg, transform, filter, apply, agg. Tempo: 3 min. -->\n",
        "<!-- ::: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Inspecting groups directly"
      ],
      "id": "dd8f2a13"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "for key, group in chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\"):\n",
        "    print(key, group.shape)"
      ],
      "id": "7fd7a905",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\").get_group(\"BRENT\").head()"
      ],
      "id": "bd2cded6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Inspecting groups is useful for debugging the split before applying a summary.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Iteration é didática e de diagnóstico; não substitui operações vetorizadas. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Grouping by mappings and functions"
      ],
      "id": "6bd44068"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "region_map = {\"BRENT\": \"Atlantic\", \"WTI\": \"Americas\", \"TTF\": \"Atlantic\"}\n",
        "latest.groupby(region_map).mean()"
      ],
      "id": "fa3f754a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Grouping keys can be columns, arrays, mappings, functions, or index levels.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Mostre que groupby é mais geral do que “agrupar por coluna”. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Optimized methods before custom aggregators"
      ],
      "id": "0669b268"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def peak_to_peak(series):\n",
        "    return series.max() - series.min()\n",
        "\n",
        "chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\")[\"price\"].agg(\n",
        "    mean=\"mean\", median=\"median\", peak_to_peak=peak_to_peak\n",
        ").round(2)"
      ],
      "id": "b407cfb8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Built-in group methods are usually clearer and faster than custom Python functions.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Use função customizada apenas para estatística não disponível. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Different functions for different columns"
      ],
      "id": "cec90b4b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\").agg({\n",
        "    \"price\": [\"mean\", \"std\"],\n",
        "    \"volume\": [\"sum\", \"median\"]\n",
        "}).round(2)"
      ],
      "id": "7d6e4b93",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "This syntax is compact but creates hierarchical column labels; named aggregation is often easier to communicate.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Mostre o MultiIndex nas colunas e por que named aggregation é preferível em entregáveis. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Grouping by index level"
      ],
      "id": "bae97038"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "indexed_ready = chart_ready.set_index([\"category\", \"instrument\"])\n",
        "indexed_ready.groupby(level=\"category\")[[\"price\", \"volume\"]].mean().round(2)"
      ],
      "id": "8074d9cf",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Grouping by an index level is useful after reshaping or hierarchical indexing.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Conecte capítulo 8 ao 10. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Quantile analysis within groups"
      ],
      "id": "9fd5bd50"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "chart_ready[\"volume_quantile\"] = chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\")[\"volume\"].transform(\n",
        "    lambda s: pd.qcut(s.rank(method=\"first\"), q=min(3, s.notna().sum()),\n",
        "                      labels=False, duplicates=\"drop\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "chart_ready.loc[:, [\"instrument\", \"volume\", \"volume_quantile\"]].head()"
      ],
      "id": "de208b46",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Quantile bins describe relative position within each group, not common absolute thresholds.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Diferencie quantile bins por instrumento de limites absolutos de volume. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plotting and Visualization\n",
        "\n",
        "## Visualization begins with the question\n",
        "\n",
        "| Question | Frequent starting point |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| How does a value evolve? | line |\n",
        "| How do categories compare? | bar or dot plot |\n",
        "| What is the distribution? | histogram, ECDF, box plot |\n",
        "| How do two quantities relate? | scatter plot |\n",
        "| How does a matrix vary? | heatmap |\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "É uma heurística, não uma regra absoluta. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Figure and Axes"
      ],
      "id": "51c9b833"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 8,
        "fig-height": 4.5
      },
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "ax.plot([1, 2, 3], [2, 5, 4], marker=\"o\")\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"A Figure contains one or more Axes\",\n",
        "       xlabel=\"Observation\", ylabel=\"Value\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "ffcb7a6e",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "- `Figure`: complete canvas;\n",
        "- `Axes`: one plotting region;\n",
        "- methods on `ax`: plot and customize.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Axes não é apenas um eixo; é a região que contém os eixos x e y. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## A technically correct but invalid chart"
      ],
      "id": "8f6d7ff5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 8,
        "fig-height": 4.5
      },
      "source": [
        "ax = summary.plot.bar(x=\"instrument\", y=\"mean_price\",\n",
        "                      legend=False, color=\"#4472C4\")\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"Mean synthetic price by instrument\",\n",
        "       xlabel=\"Instrument\", ylabel=\"Mean price in original units\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "b52f7023",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "> The code works, but the bars mix USD/bbl and EUR/MWh.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Integração simples com pandas não garante comparação válida. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Compare compatible units"
      ],
      "id": "6688040c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 10,
        "fig-height": 5
      },
      "source": [
        "crude = chart_ready.loc[chart_ready[\"category\"].eq(\"Crude oil\")]\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.lineplot(data=crude, x=\"date\", y=\"price\",\n",
        "             hue=\"instrument\", style=\"price_imputed\",\n",
        "             markers=True, dashes=False, ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"Synthetic crude-oil prices\",\n",
        "       xlabel=\"Date\", ylabel=\"Price (USD/bbl)\")\n",
        "ax.legend(title=\"Instrument / imputed\", frameon=False)\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "831e201a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "A comparação agora usa a mesma unidade e identifica imputações. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Distribution before summary"
      ],
      "id": "6f16804d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 9,
        "fig-height": 4.7
      },
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.boxplot(data=chart_ready, x=\"instrument\", y=\"price_z\",\n",
        "            hue=\"instrument\", palette=\"colorblind\", legend=False, ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"Within-instrument standardized price distributions\",\n",
        "       xlabel=\"Instrument\", ylabel=\"Price z-score\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "e267c52c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Explique mediana, quartis e whiskers. Pontos extremos não são automaticamente erros. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Relationship and semantic mappings"
      ],
      "id": "9ca550dc"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 9,
        "fig-height": 4.7
      },
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.scatterplot(data=chart_ready, x=\"volume\", y=\"return_pct\",\n",
        "                hue=\"instrument\", style=\"price_imputed\", alpha=0.8, ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.axhline(0, color=\"0.4\", linewidth=1)\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"Volume and daily return in synthetic observations\",\n",
        "       xlabel=\"Volume\", ylabel=\"Daily return (%)\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "c6860397",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Hue identifica instrumento e style torna imputação visível. Evite inferir causalidade. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Heatmaps for grouped matrices"
      ],
      "id": "f3ace2c2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 9,
        "fig-height": 4.7
      },
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.heatmap(weekly_price, cmap=\"vlag\", center=0,\n",
        "            annot=True, fmt=\".2f\", ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"Weekly mean standardized price\",\n",
        "       xlabel=\"Week\", ylabel=\"Instrument\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "f025e02a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Paleta divergente e centro zero correspondem ao significado do z-score. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Show uncertainty and coverage"
      ],
      "id": "a331f5bf"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "return_summary = (\n",
        "    chart_ready.groupby(\"instrument\", as_index=False)\n",
        "    .agg(mean_return=(\"return_pct\", \"mean\"),\n",
        "         sd_return=(\"return_pct\", \"std\"),\n",
        "         n=(\"return_pct\", \"count\"))\n",
        ")\n",
        "return_summary[\"se_return\"] = (\n",
        "    return_summary[\"sd_return\"] / np.sqrt(return_summary[\"n\"])\n",
        ").fillna(0.0)\n",
        "return_summary.round(3)"
      ],
      "id": "0e5b5997",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Erro-padrão não é dispersão dos dados nem intervalo causal. N deve ser mostrado ou auditável. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Error bars"
      ],
      "id": "7c98ee0b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 8,
        "fig-height": 4.5
      },
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "ax.errorbar(return_summary[\"instrument\"], return_summary[\"mean_return\"],\n",
        "            yerr=return_summary[\"se_return\"], fmt=\"o\", capsize=5,\n",
        "            color=\"#0072B2\")\n",
        "ax.axhline(0, color=\"0.4\", linewidth=1)\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"Mean daily return and standard error\",\n",
        "       xlabel=\"Instrument\", ylabel=\"Daily return (%)\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "044b6365",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Use para ensinar comunicação de incerteza descritiva. Dados sintéticos e amostra curta limitam interpretação. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Titles, labels, annotations, and legends\n",
        "\n",
        "A complete chart should answer:\n",
        "\n",
        "- What is being shown?\n",
        "- Over which population or sample?\n",
        "- In which units?\n",
        "- Which visual channels encode variables?\n",
        "- What feature deserves attention?\n",
        "- What limitation constrains interpretation?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Títulos devem comunicar a mensagem, mas não exagerar a evidência. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Accessibility and restraint\n",
        "\n",
        "- use sufficient contrast;\n",
        "- avoid relying only on color;\n",
        "- label axes with units;\n",
        "- remove redundant legends;\n",
        "- use direct and informative titles;\n",
        "- annotate only relevant evidence;\n",
        "- avoid 3D effects and decorative distortion.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Acessibilidade melhora precisão e reduz ambiguidade. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ## Checkpoint 4 -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- Choose and justify a chart for: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- 1. evolution of one instrument; -->\n",
        "<!-- 2. distribution of returns by instrument; -->\n",
        "<!-- 3. relationship between volume and return; -->\n",
        "<!-- 4. weekly standardized values; -->\n",
        "<!-- 5. proportions by category. -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- State the unit and one interpretive limitation. -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!-- ::: {.notes} -->\n",
        "<!-- Possíveis respostas: linha, box/violin, scatter, heatmap, barras proporcionais. Avalie coerência entre pergunta, resumo e gráfico. Tempo: 4 min. -->\n",
        "<!-- ::: -->\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Choose the visual channel deliberately\n",
        "\n",
        "| Data property | Strong visual channel |\n",
        "|---|---|\n",
        "| quantitative magnitude | aligned position |\n",
        "| ordered time | horizontal position and connection |\n",
        "| category | position, color, or shape |\n",
        "| distribution | position plus density or intervals |\n",
        "| uncertainty | intervals, bands, or distributions |\n",
        "\n",
        "Use color to support structure, not to compensate for weak comparisons.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Apresente como orientação baseada em percepção, não regra universal. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Line plots require meaningful order"
      ],
      "id": "daa3b1ee"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 9,
        "fig-height": 4.5
      },
      "source": [
        "brent_line = chart_ready.loc[chart_ready[\"instrument\"].eq(\"BRENT\")].sort_values(\"date\")\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "ax.plot(brent_line[\"date\"], brent_line[\"price\"], marker=\"o\", color=\"#0072B2\")\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"A line encodes ordered continuity\",\n",
        "       xlabel=\"Date\", ylabel=\"Price (USD/bbl)\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "83c5af24",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Linha conecta observações e implica ordem. Não use linha para categorias nominais sem ordem. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Bars need a meaningful baseline"
      ],
      "id": "9a342b1b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 8,
        "fig-height": 4.5
      },
      "source": [
        "crude_summary = crude.groupby(\"instrument\", as_index=False).agg(\n",
        "    mean_price=(\"price\", \"mean\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.barplot(data=crude_summary, x=\"instrument\", y=\"mean_price\", color=\"#4472C4\", ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set_ylim(0, None)\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"Mean crude-oil price\", xlabel=\"Instrument\", ylabel=\"Mean price (USD/bbl)\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "69344799",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Because bar length encodes magnitude, a zero baseline is normally required.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Compare com dot plot quando diferenças pequenas são o foco. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Histograms depend on bin choices"
      ],
      "id": "3fdcfe0a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 9,
        "fig-height": 4.5
      },
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, sharey=True)\n",
        "axes[0].hist(chart_ready[\"return_pct\"].dropna(), bins=4, color=\"#4472C4\")\n",
        "axes[1].hist(chart_ready[\"return_pct\"].dropna(), bins=10, color=\"#4472C4\")\n",
        "axes[0].set(title=\"4 bins\", xlabel=\"Return (%)\", ylabel=\"Frequency\")\n",
        "axes[1].set(title=\"10 bins\", xlabel=\"Return (%)\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "dfc5b7bd",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The apparent shape changes with bin width and sample size.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Ensine sensibilidade a bins. Para amostras pequenas, ECDF ou pontos individuais podem ser mais transparentes. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Density and ECDF answer different questions"
      ],
      "id": "5021e7da"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 9,
        "fig-height": 4.5
      },
      "source": [
        "fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2)\n",
        "sns.kdeplot(data=chart_ready, x=\"price_z\", hue=\"instrument\", common_norm=False, ax=axes[0])\n",
        "sns.ecdfplot(data=chart_ready, x=\"price_z\", hue=\"instrument\", ax=axes[1])\n",
        "axes[0].set(title=\"Smoothed density\", xlabel=\"Price z-score\", ylabel=\"Density\")\n",
        "axes[1].set(title=\"Empirical cumulative distribution\", xlabel=\"Price z-score\", ylabel=\"Cumulative share\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "13d83ddf",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "KDE depende de bandwidth; ECDF preserva todos os pontos sem bins ou smoothing. Tempo: 4 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Faceting prevents incompatible overlays"
      ],
      "id": "f5eb33b8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 10,
        "fig-height": 4.8
      },
      "source": [
        "facet = sns.relplot(\n",
        "    data=chart_ready, x=\"date\", y=\"price\",\n",
        "    col=\"price_unit\", hue=\"instrument\", kind=\"line\",\n",
        "    marker=\"o\", facet_kws={\"sharey\": False}, height=4, aspect=1.15\n",
        ")\n",
        "facet.set_axis_labels(\"Date\", \"Price in stated unit\")\n",
        "facet.figure.suptitle(\"Separate panels preserve unit context\", y=1.05)\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "1a763538",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Facets separam unidades, mas sharey=False dificulta comparar magnitude vertical entre painéis. Declare essa limitação. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Regression lines are models, not decorations"
      ],
      "id": "049af122"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "fig-width": 8,
        "fig-height": 4.5
      },
      "source": [
        "plot_reg = chart_ready.dropna(subset=[\"volume\", \"return_pct\"])\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots()\n",
        "sns.regplot(data=plot_reg, x=\"volume\", y=\"return_pct\",\n",
        "            scatter_kws={\"alpha\": 0.7}, line_kws={\"color\": \"#D55E00\"}, ax=ax)\n",
        "ax.set(title=\"A fitted line summarizes an assumed relationship\",\n",
        "       xlabel=\"Volume\", ylabel=\"Daily return (%)\")\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "id": "a67540de",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "A regression line does not establish causality and may conceal group structure.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Destaque amostra pequena, agrupamento ignorado e causalidade. Tempo: 3 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Legends, direct labels, and redundant encodings\n",
        "\n",
        "A legend is useful when:\n",
        "\n",
        "- several series share one plotting area;\n",
        "- labels would otherwise overlap;\n",
        "- color or style has a clear semantic mapping.\n",
        "\n",
        "Prefer direct labels when a small number of series can be identified at their endpoints. Combine color and marker shape when accessibility requires redundancy.\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.notes}\n",
        "Discuta custo cognitivo de mover os olhos entre linhas e legenda. Tempo: 2 min.\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## References\n",
        "\n",
